  id: clues-school
  displayName: The school trip
  description: Thirty children, four adults, one incident
  glyph: ST
  accentIndex: 1
  enabled: 1
  premium: 0
  freshness: 0
  reviewBy: 
  clues:
  - id: c69
    kind: 0
    text: The coach left fifteen minutes early and nobody will say who told the driver.
  - id: c70
    kind: 0
    text: All the packed lunches were swapped between bags.
  - id: c71
    kind: 0
    text: Someone pressed every button in the lift at the museum.
  - id: c72
    kind: 0
    text: The gift shop reports one missing pencil and a great deal of guilt.
  - id: c73
    kind: 0
    text: A worksheet has been filled in with answers from a completely different trip.
  - id: c74
    kind: 0
    text: The fire alarm went off during the guided tour and nobody was cooking.
  - id: c75
    kind: 0
    text: Someone has drawn a moustache on the laminated map.
  - id: c76
    kind: 0
    text: The head count came back one too many, twice.
  - id: c77
    kind: 1
    text: You did the register twice. Exactly one of {a} and {b} answered late.
  - id: c78
    kind: 1
    text: Two people were last onto the coach. One of {a} and {b} is involved.
  - id: c79
    kind: 1
    text: You checked the buddy pairs. Exactly one of {a} and {b} broke theirs.
  - id: c80
    kind: 2
    text: You were at the back of the group and saw it happen. {fact}
  - id: c81
    kind: 2
    text: You were counting heads and something did not add up. {fact}
  - id: c82
    kind: 2
    text: You turned round in the gift shop at the wrong moment. {fact}
  - id: c83
    kind: 3
    text: It was reported by a very confident nine year old. {fact}
  - id: c84
    kind: 3
    text: The museum guide mentioned it on the way out. {fact}
  - id: c85
    kind: 3
    text: Somebody wrote it in the back of the trip diary. {fact}
